==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Wargod Yoshimoto''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Immortal Yoshimoto''' at level 30 using Catfruit and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Use this cat as a generalist sniper, similar to [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Mina]] but with more HP and longer CD. Yoshimoto's [[Long Distance]] ability allows him to snipe the base in stages with a high health boss with low pushing power. His wide [[Hitbox#Subdivisions|effective range]] makes up for his unimpressive DPS, allowing him to hit a big chunk of the enemy army most of the time.

Yoshimoto's ability allows him to [[Weaken|Weaken]] Dark enemies, which makes any tanks or tanky meatshields that are supposed to protect the cat army considerably more effective, as well as greatly lowering the danger posed by the likes of [[Tackey]], [[Two Can]], [[Director Kurosawah]], or any other Dark enemy whose attacks can be expected to hit the army regardless.

==='''True Form'''===
Immortal Yoshimoto is a big improvement over his Evolved Form, as he can now almost perma-Weaken Dark enemies (completely with all [[Void Fruit]]), all while standing at a safer distance. This is a simple, but big improvement to his performance. He also gets better health that allows him to tank the near-unavoidable Tackey shots much better, among the many other benefits granted by this improvement.

=== '''Talents''' ===
'''Target [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]]''' is quite powerful, as Immortal Yoshimoto's [[Strong Against|Strong]] ability lets him survive enemy surges and his Weaken and high piercing range let him protect your entire army quite well, though he needs [[Cat Combo]]s to have full uptime, and other units must be used to get around Shields. Besides that, '''Attack''' and '''HP Buff''' are always good, [[Survive|Survive]] is costly but a nice assurance in case things go wrong. Lastly, '''Resist Freeze''' can help against several Aku enemies (like [[Ackey]] and [[Wicked Face]]), though it is extremely situational against Dark enemies, so it generally is not worth the high cost.

=== '''Ultra Talents''' ===
'''[[Surge Attack#Counter-Surge|Counter-Surge]]''' and '''Resist Surge''' only make sense in tandem. With Weaken as his primary ability, this aims to take advantage of enemy Surge Attacks to debuff and damage enemies. Against Aku specifically, this Talent sees excellent usage against [[Sinner Snache]] and [[Condemned Peng]] spam, where Yoshimoto is capable of taking full advantage of his high effective HP at Lv.60 (408,000 in most cases, as Death Surges cannot be Weakened). Think of it as an alternate take on [[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Phantasmal Nobunaga]]'s abilities. That being said, they are extremely costly in NP for what they do, and oftentimes the crowd-control goes to waste on Shielded enemies. This isn't mentioning how situational the benefits of having these abilities can be, as a fair amount of Aku don't have Death Surges or Surge Attacks to begin with. It is also inapplicable to most Dark enemies, since they seldom rely on Surge Attacks aside from those in mixed stages. Invest at your own discretion; these Ultra Talents aren't bad per se.

'''Cost Down''' is a much more clear-cut investment, but far lower priority than the other two Ultra Talents if you plan on fully speccing into him. These are simple quality-of-life improvements that he can go without, especially considering the fact that his price tag isn't a pressing concern.

==='''Orb'''===
Strong Against Aku or Dark for better performance all around. You can also go with a Defense Orb if you want to prioritize his survivability instead. For Ability Orbs, Berserker Orb is a very good option, since he's going to be netting many kills thanks to his high survivability.

Surge Resist is his best option if you plan on investing into his Ultra Talents. You can gain up to 95% resistance if you leave his Surge Resist Talent at Lv.9 and equip either an S-grade, or A- and B-grade Surge Resist Orbs; this still allows his Counter-Surge to activate while basically giving him complete immunity to Surge Attacks. With an S-grade, it is recommended utilize the second Orb slot for either a Berserker or Strong Against Aku/Dark Orb.

You are still able to gain high resistance by giving him A- and C-grade Surge Resist Orbs for 90% resistance (or just an A-grade for 80%) with Lv.10 Talents if you have already fully-specced into his Ultra Talents—or if investing so many precious Ability Orbs into Surge Resist sounds too deranged for your liking. This still grants him respectably high effective HP against Surge Attacks.

'''The [[Ototo Corps#Waterblast|Waterblast]] Style's Surge Resistance applies multiplicatively! There's no disadvantage to using it.'''

